00:16:37.590 --> 00:16:45.060
Well, a thousand shares times 40, that's $40,000. You were going to buy a thousand shares?

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:50.680
I'm a plunger. Now, if you don't have the cash, well, a check or a trading stamp for you.

00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:59.860
Hey, would you like to earn $5? $5? Yes, all you have to do is to get me a telephone.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:06.860
operator a telephone operator dog gone if i don't believe that i got one on my truck on your truck

00:17:07.530 --> 00:17:14.200
just another service of the haney curbside employment agency stand back

00:17:20.550 --> 00:17:29.280
now you wanted a telephone operator you say yeah he's a cocktail waitress she's a fandango dancer

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:38.730
and he's an atomic scientist on the leave of absence I was sure that I had a

00:17:38.730 --> 00:17:42.830
telephone operator on the truck when I left home this morning she must have

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:48.190
bounced off someplace don't worry I'll find her all right folks we're moving

00:17:48.190 --> 00:17:54.840
out and just remember ten percent of each pot goes to the Haney curbside

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:55.960
Employment Agency.

00:18:00.030 --> 00:18:02.110
8 o'clock, when are we going to go home?

00:18:02.450 --> 00:18:03.690
We can't go home.

00:18:03.870 --> 00:18:04.950
This is a phone company.

00:18:05.090 --> 00:18:07.030
Somebody's got to be here 24 hours a day.

00:18:07.270 --> 00:18:09.390
But you don't know how to run a switchboard.

00:18:09.750 --> 00:18:11.850
All you do is sit there and stare at it.

00:18:12.250 --> 00:18:14.790
Well, somebody's got to be on duty to stare at it.

00:18:15.870 --> 00:18:18.850
Now, forsaking all the others, what is your main problem?

00:18:19.580 --> 00:18:22.180
My main problem is I can take the incoming calls,

00:18:22.320 --> 00:18:25.200
but I don't know which holes to plug in to get them the person they want.

00:18:26.490 --> 00:18:27.810
I think I got a solution.

00:18:28.110 --> 00:18:29.970
I got a solution to get a hold of...

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:33.700
Roy Trennel, get him stoned, get him into a poker game with a mark deck, and deal the

00:18:33.700 --> 00:18:34.580
company back to him.

00:18:40.340 --> 00:18:44.710
Vandal Douglas, who stood up in Congress, three overboard.

00:18:45.810 --> 00:18:48.110
Well, I was much more of a tea dumper in those days.

00:18:49.230 --> 00:18:49.610
Oliver!

00:18:50.210 --> 00:18:53.510
Lisa, you just sit there and stare at that board and let me try to figure a way out of

00:18:53.510 --> 00:18:53.970
this mess.

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:08.340
I got it figured out!

00:19:08.740 --> 00:19:08.980
What?

00:19:09.140 --> 00:19:10.270
Who do you want to talk to?

00:19:11.410 --> 00:19:14.970
Pick a name, and read what it says, and I plug them in for you.

00:19:15.760 --> 00:19:17.860
Oh, uh, Newt Carly?

00:19:18.610 --> 00:19:22.190
Newt Carly, he's a three by three.

00:19:22.490 --> 00:19:24.070
One, two, three, one, two, three.

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:28.790
Hello? Mr. Carly?

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:29.660
Good.

00:19:30.030 --> 00:19:32.330
I just want to show my husband I know where you were.

00:19:34.340 --> 00:19:37.760
Uh, well, Drucker, four or two.

00:19:38.660 --> 00:19:40.580
Oh, one, two, three, four, one, two.

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:45.680
Hello, Mr. Drucker?

00:19:46.340 --> 00:19:49.500
I just wanted to make sure that you are where you're supposed to be.

00:19:49.700 --> 00:19:53.320
But now, it works good, doesn't it?

00:19:54.270 --> 00:19:55.130
Yeah, but how...

00:19:55.130 --> 00:19:59.250
While you were schnoozhing, I called up everybody and I asked them who they were.

00:19:59.410 --> 00:19:59.970
And then I...

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:04.560
I counted how many rows down and how many rows across they were on the punch board.

00:20:04.740 --> 00:20:05.500
Uh, switchboard.

00:20:05.700 --> 00:20:05.840
No.

00:20:06.460 --> 00:20:07.200
Punch board.

00:20:07.990 --> 00:20:09.490
I got the idea from my father.

00:20:09.840 --> 00:20:12.120
He was the head of the Budapest Punch Board Company.

00:20:13.100 --> 00:20:14.780
Do you know what a punch board is?

00:20:15.080 --> 00:20:17.100
Yes, it's something you take a chance on.

00:20:17.240 --> 00:20:19.820
You, uh, you select the number you want and then you punch it out.

00:20:20.020 --> 00:20:21.420
That's how my father got rich.

00:20:21.760 --> 00:20:24.240
He never put any lucky numbers in his punch board.

00:20:25.720 --> 00:20:27.140
Lisa, your punch board is ringing.

00:20:30.440 --> 00:20:33.360
Hello? This is the Hootersville phone company.

00:20:33.850 --> 00:20:35.820
Who do you want? Mr. Bannett?

00:20:36.060 --> 00:20:37.280
One moment, Polly, yes.

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:39.780
Mr. Bannett, this is a two by five.

00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:42.040
One, two, one, two, three, four, five.

00:20:44.280 --> 00:20:45.540
What if there's something in there?

00:20:48.480 --> 00:20:51.100
Number 74. You have just punched the lucky number.

00:20:51.560 --> 00:20:54.880
First prize, the Hootersville phone company.

00:20:55.060 --> 00:20:56.160
Good night, I...

00:21:00.600 --> 00:21:06.580
Get the 3x6 for Mr. 4x2.

